Subject: web: let the browser shim run below a reverse proxy sub-path

Why: the web client only works at the site root. The shim calls the Host with
root-absolute paths (/api/..., /chat, /events) and sends logout to /connect, so
behind a reverse proxy that serves Cindy under a prefix (for example a NAS app
gateway at /app/cindy/) every Host request leaves the prefix and fails. The
shim now prefixes these paths with window.__CINDY_BASE__, which the proxy sets
before the shim loads (a trailing slash is ignored). Unset or empty keeps
today's paths exactly; a value that is not a same-origin path (URL, //host,
backslash) is ignored. The renderer's own assets are handled by building it
with Vite --base; nothing in this patch is specific to one proxy.
Upstream: issue https://github.com/makecindy/cindy/issues/10614, PR not yet
submitted (branch feat/web-base-path).
Remove when: upstream web shim supports a path prefix (by this or another
mechanism) without this patch.
